o@icebubble.org  escreveu:
> I was just comparing the new edition of the official Lojban Reference
> Grammar (CLL v1.1) with my annotated(/corrected) bound copy of the
> book... and I find myself rather disappointed.  A few of the errors in
> v1.0 were corrected, but most of the errors, omissions, ambiguities, and
> confusing passages in v1.0 were retained in v1.1.  I had hoped that
> these errors would be caught, and that the new edition of the CLL would
> be clear, correct, and intelligible.
>=20
> Here's just one example off the top of my head: In section 10.4, both
> CLLv1.0 and v1.1 state that a temporal tense is expressed before a
> spatial tense.  But the formal grammar (EBNF Rule 972, yacc Rule 979)
> allows them to occur in either order.  The text is still wrong.  And
> there are many other examples.
>=20
> Could anyone tell me why all these problems weren't corrected in CLL
> v1.1?

Because those who publish the CLL are not superbeings? Hint: continue unoff=
icially at https://lojban.pw in a hope that the officials catch up.

